meta {
  name: 63 Registration Settings
  seq: 63
}

docs {
  # Registration Settings

  Registration › Registration Settings — the LIMS Settings doc's "Registration
  Module" section: general toggles, quotation validity, charges & deductions,
  cancellation & refund, referral & staff permissions, billing-menu overrides,
  and the appointment/patient-merge toggles. Tenant-scoped **and**
  branch-level (RLS) — one row per branch, branch taken from the caller's
  active profile (never the body):

  - **GET `/enums`** — allowed values for `General_DefaultPaymentMode`
    (`PaymentMode`) and `Quotation_QuotationValidityUnit`
    (`RepeatIntervalUnit`).
  - **GET** — the active branch's Registration settings row, auto-created with
    Prisma defaults on first access (never 404s).
  - **PUT** — upserts the active branch's Registration settings (a partial
    patch — omitted fields keep their previously-saved value, or the schema
    default on first save). Server-side rules: every `Minimum*Percent` must
    not exceed its paired `Maximum*Percent` (TDS, discount, line-item
    discount); at most one of `ChargesAndDeductions_AllowOrderDiscountOnly` /
    `AllowLineDiscountOnly` / `AllowBothOrderAndLineDiscount` may be `true`.

  Field names follow `<Heading>_<Setting>` (e.g.
  `ReferralAndStaffPermissions_AllowAddReferral`) to mirror the source doc 1:1.

  ID-generation config (Order/Quotation/Appointment/Patient-UMID external ids
  — prefix/separator/suffix/number-length/reset-cycle + a live preview) is a
  separate sibling resource — see "Registration Id Sequences" below.

  All routes are business-authenticated (`Bearer {{businessAccessToken}}`);
  tenant from the JWT, branch from the active profile. `PUT` is audited under
  `AuditModule.REGISTRATION_SETTINGS`.
}
